# Architecture

## Structure

- Organize each layer by feature (e.g., `Domain/User/`, `Application/User/`, `Infrastructure/User/`)
- Put code shared across features in each layer's `Shared/` (e.g., `Domain/Shared/`); duplicating code across features is acceptable, so propose and get approval before moving code to `Shared/`

## Domain

- `Domain/` holds entities, value objects, enums, domain exceptions, and repository interfaces

## Application

- `Application/` has one directory per use case, containing a handler and its input (e.g., `User/CreateUser/CreateUserHandler`, `User/CreateUser/CreateUserInput`)
- Read-only queries go through a `*ReaderInterface` that returns `*Record` DTOs; put the interface and records in the feature directory of `Application/` (e.g., `Application/User/UserReaderInterface`, `Application/User/UserRecord`) and the implementation in `Infrastructure/`

## Infrastructure

- `Infrastructure/` holds controllers, Doctrine repository and reader implementations, security (authenticators and voters), console commands, Twig extensions, and other framework integrations
- Rely on autowiring to bind interfaces to their only implementation; configure the binding in `config/services.yaml` only when an interface has multiple implementations
